    "docs/user-guide/analysis-tools.md",
    "# Explore coverage and analysis tools\n\nThese workflows use the active map and selected capture. Availability depends on the Builder configuration, data coverage, and the services connected to the experience. Start by [opening a capture](../getting-started.md) and checking the [image information](image-information.md).\n\n| Goal | Workflow | What to check |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Review imagery coverage | Open **Analyze Coverage** and follow the coverage guide in the viewer. | Coverage describes available imagery, which can change with filters and zoom. |\n| Plan a capture route | Set the start and end points in the route controls, select a configured provider, and generate a route before opening the preview or exporting GPX. | Preview is a simulation. Check the route against local travel conditions before using the export. |\n| Explore sequence elevation | Enable the elevation profile for a selected sequence and use its indicator to follow the confirmed capture. | Camera altitude and terrain data are estimates. |\n| Inspect capture-time sunlight | Enable solar modeling on a capture with a timestamp and location. | The calculation uses capture metadata. The scene and photograph can show different lighting. |\n| Explore reconstructed geometry | Open the point-cloud controls on a capture with an available reconstruction. Inspect the result and select the appropriate tool before measuring or exporting. | Check alignment and calibration before relying on measurements or exported coordinates. |\n\n!!! tip \"Choose the right view\"\n    If a map tool is unavailable, check the selected capture and the active map type. Some point-cloud analysis and scene-lighting controls depend on a 3D view.\n\n## Related references\n\n- [Coverage readiness and startup](../development/coverage-readiness.md) and [routing validation](../development/routing-validation.md)\n- [Elevation profile workflow](../development/sequence-profile-workflow.md) and [solar model workflow](../development/solar-model-workflow.md)\n- [Point-cloud ownership and validation](../development/point-cloud.md)\n",
    "# Explore coverage and analysis tools\n\nThese workflows use the active map and selected capture. Availability depends on the Builder configuration, data coverage, and the services connected to the experience. Start by [opening a capture](../getting-started.md) and checking the [image information](image-information.md).\n\n| Goal | Workflow | What to check |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Review imagery coverage | Open **Analyze Coverage** and follow the coverage guide in the viewer. | Coverage describes available imagery, which can change with filters and zoom. |\n| Plan a capture route | Set the start and end points in the route controls, select a configured provider, and generate a route before opening the preview or exporting GPX. | Preview is a simulation. Check the route against local travel conditions before using the export. |\n| Explore sequence elevation | Enable the elevation profile for a selected sequence and use its indicator to follow the confirmed capture. | Camera altitude and terrain data are estimates. |\n| Inspect capture-time sunlight | Enable solar modeling on a capture with a timestamp and location. | The calculation uses capture metadata. The scene and photograph can show different lighting. |\n| Explore reconstructed geometry | Open the point-cloud controls on a capture with an available reconstruction. Inspect the result and select the appropriate tool before measuring or exporting. | Check alignment and calibration before relying on measurements or exported coordinates. |\n\n!!! tip \"Choose the right view\"\n    If a map tool is unavailable, check the selected capture and the active map type. Some point-cloud analysis and scene-lighting controls depend on a 3D view.\n"
